I0918 16:09:33.487087       1 strace.go:567] [   1:  12] agent-probe E write(0x6 /tmp/summary.txt, 0x16d83bb7fb00 "RFC 8446 specifies version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol, which provides communications security over the Internet by enabling client/server applications to detect eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery. It redesigns the handshake to reduce latency (enabling 1-round-trip and optional 0-round-trip connection setup) and removes support for weak, obsolete cryptographic primitives and legacy features such as static RSA/Diffie-Hellman key exchange, compression, renegotiation, and many older cipher suites. All handshake messages after the ServerHello are now encrypted, improving privacy and reducing the amount of information exposed to network observers. The specification defines a simplified set of authenticated encryption (AEAD) cipher suites, mandates forward secrecy via (EC)DHE key exchange, and details session resumption, 0-RTT data, key updates, and post-handshake authentication mechanisms. Overall, RFC 8446 obsoletes RFC 5246 (TLS 1.2) and related documents, aiming to make TLS 1.3"..., 0x447)
